  "title": "Vowels 2: উ ঊ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**উ** and **ঊ** are both `u` as in *food*: a 'short u' and a 'long u' that **sound the same** in speech, just like ই and ঈ. The long **ঊ** has one more stroke.\n\nLearn the spelling with the word:\n\n- **উ**ট (camel), **উ**কিল (lawyer)\n- **ঊ**রু (thigh), **ঊ**ষা (dawn)\n\nঊ is rare at the start of a word, so these are two of the few you'll see.\n\nWatch out: উ looks a lot like the consonant ড (`d`) that you'll meet later; ড has a notch in its top line.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-u",
      "bn": "উ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (short-u letter)",
      "notes": "Name: hroshsho-u (হ্রস্ব উ). Sounds the same as ঊ in modern speech."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-uu",
      "bn": "ঊ",
      "tr": "u",
      "en": "u as in 'food' (long-u letter)",
      "notes": "Name: dirgho-u (দীর্ঘ ঊ). Same sound as উ; it is উ with an extra loop on top-right. Rare at the start of words."
    },
    {
      "id": "ut",
